## Scope and counts

This page uses the knowledge-base export dated 4 October 2026, not the current live queue.
The report export repeats IDs where its pages overlap. Count each report ID once, then
filter to the merged ticket; matching subjects do not identify duplicates.

The published dataset is a privacy-reduced projection: report bodies, subjects and browser locales
are omitted, and tenant handles are replaced consistently by aliases. The full original export
is retained locally. This preserves report IDs, counting, cause grouping and timeline inputs.
The table below computes the cause from tenant locale, form version and channel using
`causes.ts`. Intake's browser-based tag is a guess, not the grouping rule.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Two independent fixes to investigate

**Shared parser.** It reads dates month first while these tenants write day first.
For example, R-41200 describes a reminder for 7 April being sent on 4 July.
Respect the tenant's intended date order on the parser path.

**Booking form hint.** booking-v3 displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, but interprets dates using the
tenant's day-first locale. People following that hint get the wrong day and month.
This affects form reports from tenant-01, tenant-02 and tenant-09. Align the
hint with the form's interpretation; a shared-parser fix alone does not resolve this mismatch.
App and email reports from those same tenants still belong to the parser cause.

Track the causes separately: [shared parser — 379 reports](https://github.com/wojttex/mega-dev-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1)
and [booking-v3 hint mismatch — 33 reports](https://github.com/wojttex/mega-dev-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).
The engineering dispositions below come from the course update; no independent production-patch verification is claimed.

## Engineering dispositions: 5 October 2026

The [engineering update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows#engineering-update)
reports that #4471 closed on 5 October:

- **Parser: fixed.** Engineering reports `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
  [GitHub issue #1](https://github.com/wojttex/mega-dev-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1)
  is closed as completed.
- **Hint: won’t fix.** The booking-v3 form was retired.
  [GitHub issue #2](https://github.com/wojttex/mega-dev-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2)
  is closed as not planned. Retirement is not a fix to the hint.

The export ends on 4 October, so the computed table and timeline retain their historical
counts. The subsequent engineering update supplies the dispositions; it does not change
which reports were in the export or establish the cause of the ambiguous descriptions.

## Keep the one-day-move evidence visible

The desk notes mark R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344 and R-41620 as read as a one-day move.
The exported classifier files them under parser by tenant and channel, and the table's
footnote counts them there. They are already included, never five extra reports.
Their descriptions do not establish a day/month swap in every case. In particular,
the Lisbon/Toronto difference in R-41344 merits a timezone investigation. Keep these reports
for follow-up; neither suppress their wording nor call a third defect confirmed from this export.

## Received is different from merged

Reports arrived from April onward. The July merge spike combines an older backlog; it does
not mean those reports first arrived in July. The paired chart separates received time from
merge time. Reports continued through the export date; this export says nothing about the
queue after that date.

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Replace subject-only triage

The [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) points to
[accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject), last reviewed in June 2024.
That guidance is stale under the knowledge base's review rule. Preserve accepted decision
0001 as history; a new accepted decision must replace it rather than silently editing it.

Use the same cause, not a normalized subject, to decide whether reports belong together:

- App versus email for the same day-first tenant can be the same parser issue.
- The same subject for one booking-v3 tenant can be two issues: form hint versus app parser.
- The same subject and form channel can differ by tenant form version.
- Different subjects can still describe the same booking-v3 hint mismatch.
- An unknown tenant cannot be assigned a cause safely; investigate before merging.

<DedupeExplorer />

This page proposes the replacement guidance and keeps the prior decision visible.
It does not establish that the desk has adopted it. Re-check the live queue and tenant/form
configuration when new evidence arrives, and update counts from report IDs and computed causes.

